hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17097","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Hariz ibn Uthman al-Rahabi narrated to us, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Amir al-Alhani say: Habis ibn Sa'd al-Ta'i entered the mosque before dawn - and he had met the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and saw people praying in the front of the mosque, so he said: Show-offs, by the Lord of the Ka'bah; frighten them; whoever frightens them has obeyed Allah and His Messenger. So the people came to them and expelled them. He said: So he said: The angels pray before dawn in the front of the mosque."
